    "alternateSlug": null,
    "excerpt": "Store ayah numbers in Hafs numbering and convert only at the edges of your application.",
    "html": "<h1 id=\"section-1\">Developer usage</h1>\n<p>Keep one internal numbering axis. In this repository that axis is Kufi/Hafs: store it in your database and in your URLs, and convert only when displaying another madhhab or accepting a number from one.</p>\n<h2 id=\"section-2\">The files you need</h2>\n<ul><li><code>dist/mappings/by-counting-system/kufi-to-*.json</code> — convert a Hafs number into another madhhab.</li><li><code>dist/mappings/by-counting-system/*-to-kufi.json</code> — convert a number from another madhhab back to Hafs.</li><li><code>dist/surah-counts/*.json</code> — accepted surah totals per madhhab.</li><li><code>dist/rawis/*.json</code> — when your interface starts from a rawi name and needs its counting madhhab.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"section-3\">Read the status field</h2>\n<p>Every entry carries a <code>status</code> describing the kind of correspondence. Ignore it and you will display wrong numbers wherever ayahs merge or split.</p>\n<ul><li><code>mapped</code> — one ayah corresponds to one ayah.</li><li><code>merged</code> — this ayah joins the next one in the target madhhab; see <code>merges_with_next</code>.</li><li><code>split</code> — this ayah becomes two or more; see <code>splits_into</code>.</li><li><code>covers_multiple</code> — in a reverse file, this ayah spans several Hafs ayahs; see <code>hafs_ayahs</code>.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"section-4\">In the interface</h2>\n<p>Show madhhab names to readers rather than internal field names, and keep maintenance tables out of the reading experience. Kufan rawis share Hafs numbering, so they need no conversion at all.</p>",
