    "slug": "methodology",
    "title": "Methodology",
    "group": "curation",
    "language": "en",
    "direction": "ltr",
    "alternateSlug": "methodology-ar",
    "excerpt": "How a disputed position is recorded, and how the counts and conversion files are derived from it.",
    "html": "<h1 id=\"section-1\">Methodology</h1>\n<p>The project rests on a small, hand-edited source layer that records disputed positions only. Undisputed positions are left implicit, because they need no supporting text.</p>\n<h2 id=\"section-2\">What each position records</h2>\n<ul><li><b>The fāṣilah wording</b> — the word the position ends on, which anchors it to the text.</li><li><b>Kind</b> — the end of a Kufan ayah, or a break inside one.</li><li><b>Who counts it</b> — the counting madhhabs that treat it as a head of ayah.</li></ul>\n<p>Kufi is the reference axis because it is the numbering of the mushafs in common use, which makes referring the others back to it straightforward.</p>\n<h2 id=\"section-3\">What is derived</h2>\n<p>Surah totals per madhhab, the conversion files between madhhabs, the rawi files, and the site data are all generated from that one layer. No total is written by hand unless it is a transmitted statement.</p>\n<h2 id=\"section-4\">Mushaf display</h2>\n<p>Ayahs are numbered by the displayed madhhab, not by Hafs, unless Kufi is the displayed madhhab.</p>\n<p>Where a madhhab does not count the basmala of al-Fatiha, it is shown unnumbered in place rather than folded into ayah one.</p>\n<h2 id=\"section-5\">Validation</h2>\n<p>The test suite checks the source layer for internal consistency, checks that generated outputs match it, and checks the mushaf display for every surah in every madhhab.</p>",
